ies that he  probably was wasn't he  so I want to dig into this a little bit  more now this is by no means  comprehensive but the first thing I do  want to address is that as I said I've  seen it come up with my comment section  now I've even seen the arguments made  elsewhere you know that the the first  doctor was not misogynistic in any way  now again I don't know William  Hartnell's whole run I only know a  handful of it here and there but I can  give you an example right from the very  first episode where I'm sorry he kind of  was during an unearthly child very first  episode ever broadcast Ian and Barbara  the two school teachers who Susan is  their student and they're trying to  think something's weird with this girl's  so they followed her to this junkyard  they've seen her go into the police box  they're trying to figure out what's  going on or they they thought they saw  her go there they they're trying to  figure out what what is going on here  they brought in to the doctor and they  start questioning him and I went back  and relooked at this scene again and  there were a couple things I noticed  when Barbara suggests that she saw Susan  go into the police box the doctor is  incredibly dismissive oh you must have  imagined it when Ian says that he wants  answers the doctor doesn't dismiss him  or try and Gaslight him instead he tries  to offer him a more logical reasoned  excuse and then not very long after that  when Barbara asks the doctor basically  the same question again the doctor not  only fails to answer her but takes Ian  by the arm leads him away from her and  talks to him instead there's a very  clear dismissive attitude towards  Barbara and kind of a presumption of  authority given by the doctor towards  Ian so now this is just the first  episode and I like is that there's not a  comprehensive list of incidences like  this but if I can find something in  episode 1  I look people who love the first doctor  there is something here that having be